      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": null,
      "updated": 1771299237050,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "In these operations, the digits are moved, or shifted to the left or right. \nRegisters in a computer processor have a fixed width, so some bits will be \"shifted out \" \nof the register at one end, while the same number of bits are \"shifted in \" from the other end; \nthe difference between bit shift operators lie in how they determine the values of shifted-in bits.",
      "fontSize": 20,
      "fontFamily": 5,
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "In these operations, the digits are moved, or shifted to the left or right. \nRegisters in a computer processor have a fixed width, so some bits will be \"shifted out \" \nof the register at one end, while the same number of bits are \"shifted in \" from the other end; \nthe difference between bit shift operators lie in how they determine the values of shifted-in bits.",
      "autoResize": true,
      "lineHeight": 1.25
    },
